# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Node
node_modules/
web/dist/
.vite/

# Env & secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Containers
.lapidary-data/
volumes/

# The default storage root. deploy/compose.yaml binds ${LAPIDARY_STORAGE_ROOT:-../storage}
# into api and worker, and compose resolves that against deploy/, so an operator who sets
# nothing gets the user's own parts library right here, inside the working tree. Never
# ours to commit, and it must not sit in `git status` inviting a broad `git add`. Note
# what an ignore entry cannot do: `git clean -xfd` removes ignored files by definition,
# so a store that matters belongs outside the repository — set LAPIDARY_STORAGE_ROOT.
/storage/

# Generated
sidecar/occt-bridge/build/
crates/*/bindings/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors
.idea/
*.swp
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Third-party model archives. A 156 MB .rar was once swept into a docs commit by a broad
# `git add` and made the repository unpushable — GitHub rejects any file over 100 MB.
# Keep such archives outside the repo entirely.
*.rar

# Materialized by `cargo xtask setup` from the marketplaces .claude/settings.json
# declares. A cache of another repository, never a copy this one owns.
/.agents/skills/
/.agents/.cache/

# Transient agent worktrees — a second full checkout of this repository, created and
# removed by tooling. A broad `git add` here commits an entire copy of the tree into
# itself, which is the same accident the .rar rule above records, one order of magnitude
# larger. Never committed, never needed.
/.claude/worktrees/

# The impeccable design detector's engine: a 16 MB platform-specific binary that
# `npx impeccable install` fetches per machine. Its own hooks are written
# `[ ! -f <binary> ] || <binary> hook`, so an absent engine is a no-op rather than a
# broken session — which is what makes leaving it out of the tree safe. The skill, its
# reference material and its hooks are committed; only the compiled linux-x64 artefact
# is not, because a binary in git is forever and this one is wrong on any other arch.
.claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/bin/

# The knowledge graph graphify builds from this tree. Split, because the parts are not
# alike: one of them cost 701,555 tokens to make and the rest are a minute of CPU.
#
# **What is kept is `cache/semantic/`** — one JSON per source file, named by that file's
# SHA-256, holding the concepts and rationale a language model read out of it. It is the
# only expensive thing here, it is keyed by content rather than by path, and every
# `source_file` inside it is repository-relative, so it is correct on any clone. A file
# nobody edits never produces a new entry, which is also the git behaviour you want.
# Without it, every clone and every CI run re-pays that extraction.
#
# `GRAPH_REPORT.md`, `manifest.json` (what `--update` diffs against), the community
# labels and the cumulative token ledger come along for a few hundred KB more, and all
# four are worth reading in a diff.
/graphify-out/*
!/graphify-out/cache/
/graphify-out/cache/*
!/graphify-out/cache/semantic/
!/graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md
!/graphify-out/graph.json
!/graphify-out/manifest.json
!/graphify-out/cost.json
!/graphify-out/.graphify_labels.json
# The agent-crawlable half: index.md plus one article per community, wikilinked, every
# concept carrying the file it came from. 572 KB of markdown that diffs cleanly, and the
# reason it is here rather than regenerated is that an agent reading this repository should
# find it by looking, not by running a pipeline first.
!/graphify-out/wiki/

# Excluded, and each for its own reason rather than for being big:
#
#   graph.html          3 MB, regenerated wholesale by `graphify export html` from
#                       graph.json. A derived file that changes entirely on every build
#                       is the thing git stores worst.
#   cache/ast/          3.4 MB in a single file, and free — AST extraction is
#                       deterministic and finished in seconds. Paying git for it to
#                       avoid paying the CPU is the wrong way round.
#   cache/stat-index    absolute paths plus `mtime_ns`, so it is wrong on every other
#                       machine and after every fresh clone here.
#   .graphify_python    an absolute path to one machine's interpreter.
#   .graphify_root      the same, for the scan root.
#
# `graph.json` is kept despite being 3.7 MB and rewritten in full each build, because it
# is what `graphify query` reads — without it a clone cannot ask the graph anything until
# it rebuilds. It carries `built_at_commit`, so a reader can tell how stale it is.
# ponytail: if that churn becomes the complaint, drop it — with cache/semantic committed
# a rebuild costs no tokens and about a minute.
